codemap 8
path feature-inline-link
kind flow
author ai
group features/gui
note A step that links to another path has an 'inline' button. The reader reaches for it to read a linked path's steps in place, under the step that calls into it, instead of leaving the path being read. Pressed, the linked path's steps appear inline under the step, indented one level and numbered after it (1.2 › 1, 1.2 › 1.1), each with its own view buttons; 'un-inline' removes them. A link to a path already inlined further up shows 'inlined above' instead of a button, so a cycle of links cannot recurse.

